    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107-a5">

                <pb facs="0254" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg158"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 146 <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >bis.</hi>—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. James to Mr. Williamson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 25, 1874</date>.
                        (Received in Guatemala 2 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Arizona has sailed. I was present and
                    saw everything. The captain used every exertion to prevent the shooting, but
                    some of the passengers fired pistols and mortally wounded Commandante Gonzalez.
                    I used every exertion to prevent the outrage on Mr. Magee. Will send details by
                    mail.</p>
                <closer><signed>E. JAMES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
